cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  IELTS-API: a free, authentication-free, reproducible reference implementation
  of IELTS scoring and language-assessment analytics
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - name: IELTS-API Contributors
    website: https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API
repository-code: https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API
url: https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API
abstract: >-
  IELTS-API is a dependency-free TypeScript library and HTTP API that implements
  the arithmetic and the analytics of the International English Language Testing
  System: the official Overall Band Score rounding rule, raw-score to band-score
  conversion for Listening and Reading, the published alignment to the Common
  European Framework of Reference, analytic band descriptors, Academic Word List
  profiling, classical readability indices, a rule base of frequent learner
  errors, and a transparent glass-box estimator for Writing band scores. Every
  endpoint is free and requires no authentication of any kind, and every response
  is deterministic, so published results can be reproduced exactly.
keywords:
  - IELTS
  - language assessment
  - band score
  - CEFR
  - academic word list
  - readability
  - automated writing evaluation
  - reproducible research
  - open API
  - TypeScript
license: MIT
